  "interpretation": {
    "narrowest_safe_claim": "For the frozen six-task synthetic fixture and 3B revision-rubric condition, conjoining the deterministic gate reduced external false-ready observations from 23/48 to 13/48 with six cluster-level directional reductions (exact two-sided p=0.03125). The prespecified correct-delivery/claim-coverage guardrail failed, falling from 10/24 to 5/24, so this is not evidence of a method win or general coding efficacy.",
    "significance_status": "primary p<0.05 but guardrail failed; secondary raw p-values are exploratory and none remain significant after Holm adjustment",
    "all_valid_verdicts_ready": true,
    "invalid_response_behavior": "The model never supplied a valid BLOCKED verdict in these artifacts; non-ready rows came from 3B timeouts or 1B JSON parse failures."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Only six base-task clusters from one authored fixture family were tested; seeds repeat candidates and are not independent units.",
    "The primary 3B block has 39/72 timeout failures, and every valid model verdict is READY; treating failures as non-ready is preregistered ITT accounting but leaves substantial attrition.",
    "The deterministic gate is metadata/revision based and is not a semantic oracle; current metadata permits overbroad and test-tampering false-ready cases.",
    "The hidden behavior oracle improves label independence but does not establish real repository productivity, human usefulness, or external project validity.",
    "D is a 36-unique-candidate gate diagnostic; copying it across prompt/seed cells would create a denominator error and was not used here for inference.",
    "A significant primary p-value cannot be reported as a method win when the predeclared correct-delivery/coverage guardrail fails."
  ]
